{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454854-other-way-to-use-hunger-in-v5","id":1454854,"title":"Other way to use hunger in v5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-13T17:32:09-07:00","id":1454854,"title":"Other way to use hunger in v5","content":"According to the book, the hunger is at the same time the need of blood, the beast instinct and some supernatural excitations <br /> And still from the Book to completely satisfy the hunger and get to 0 you have to feed on a mortal to death.<br /> I was wondering, would it be logic to feed on multiple mortal to satisfy our hunger? <br /> You get 2 point by feeding on a mortal without danger (for the poor prey of course) so if get 2 more points by feeding on an other mortal (eventually with help of some vampiric powers) could we get to 0 without killing any human?<br /> I'm asking because i want to play a powerfull vampire warrior with high dcore of humanity because he want to protect his family through times but being locked at hunger 3 because the only way to get lower is to kill is not really convenient and not really logic: you feed on 5 humans for a big load of blood without killing them and not enough to hurt them badly but even with that much you cannot get to 0? Hmmm...<br /> Maybe through new rules or changed one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-13-2021, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T18:31:56-07:00","id":1454856,"title":"","content":"No. The book is very clear on that 'go to 0 being a kill' is what fully satiates the Beast, and causes it to basically go dormant for a while. As you said yourself, it's the need for blood but also the Beast's desires, as well. So you have to satiate the Beast in its entirety. There are no ways to go to Hunger 0 without the kill. <br /> <br /> Also, why are you talking about locked at Hunger 3? Unless something stops you from doing multiple safe feeds (1 at a time, for example), you can reduce to Hunger 1, which is pretty trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T00:56:09-07:00","id":1454867,"title":"","content":"Easy fix: make it so you *can* get to Hunger 0 by feeding from multiple sources, but it lasts for a scene. After that, you return to Hunger 1. Adjust it up or down by increasing or decreasing the length of time you stay at Hunger 0, as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-15-2021, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T01:18:00-07:00","id":1454869,"title":"","content":"So in that case a permanent hunger at 0 would mean ingame that the beast is satisfy from killing his prey. That's a good idea, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T10:37:39-07:00","id":1455622,"title":"","content":"However, i'm not sure about how the exaltation work on the body of the vampire:<br /> The way i see it is if he's lucky he will not excite the beast or loose blood by activating a power or something else; like this time no problem, your body is unchanged but the next time oh cr*p you awakened the beast and/or loose blood to use your power, what a shame...<br /> In the v20 the blood points was clear about how work the powers, you use a portion of your blood and convert it into energy for disciplines. But in v5, with 5 levels of hunger that describe the thirst, the beast instinct, and excitation, plus a &quot;test&quot; to know if using a discipline will affect you or not only based on how lucky you are when you roll the dice...<br /> I don't know, it seems weird to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-26-2021, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T11:06:17-07:00","id":1455623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454854-other-way-to-use-hunger-in-v5?p=1455622#post1455622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, i'm not sure about how the exaltation work on the body of the vampire:<br /> The way i see it is if he's lucky he will not excite the beast or loose blood by activating a power or something else; like this time no problem, your body is unchanged but the next time oh cr*p you awakened the beast and/or loose blood to use your power, what a shame...<br /> In the v20 the blood points was clear about how work the powers, you use a portion of your blood and convert it into energy for disciplines. But in v5, with 5 levels of hunger that describe the thirst, the beast instinct, and excitation, plus a &quot;test&quot; to know if using a discipline will affect you or not only based on how lucky you are when you roll the dice...<br /> I don't know, it seems weird to me</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an alternate system. I use the V20 blood pool but add Beast Dice at the ninth through seventh (+1), sixth through fifth (+2), fourth through third (+3), second (+4) and last (+5) blood point, with +6 when you reach zero (similar to how your stats go right up at Wassail). Each of these is a Hunger Level, just like Health Levels, but giving dice instead of taking them away.<br /> <br /> When you do Beast-ly things (hunting, killing, etc) you can add your Beast Dice as a bonus. When you need to concentrate or behave like a human, you instead deduct them as a penalty.<br /> <br /> When you fill your blood pool, you're Gorged for a scene, which means no Frenzy or R\u00f6tschreck tests. After that scene is up, the Beast awakens but is weakened. You still have to test for Frenzy and R\u00f6tschreck, but have no Messy Crits or Bestial Failures (just regular crits and botches).<br /> <br /> Even when you do get a Messy Crit or Bestial Failure, they're not the end of the world. You can just spend an extra Willpower point or an extra blood point to negate it, as you overextend yourself (MC); or you can spend 1XP to ignore it completely (either MC or BF). If you do accept it, you get a little perk (extra WP or XP).<br /> <br /> More info here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1D21-VzkAM_zBUhUPIQUPtUukKU2K0ir1A8njq2S7O1Y/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...t?usp=drivesdk</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-26-2021, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T14:36:27-07:00","id":1455626,"title":"","content":"I've also thought about taking back the blood points cause it seems more accurate, but before changing the system i'm trying to understand the meaning of it.<br /> As it was explained to me earlier, the hunger is at the same time the beast instinct, represented by the default level of hunger which is higher with a powerfull blood and the need of blood for the last levels of hunger. <br /> Now i'm trying to understand what represent the exaltation test for the vampire in-game, what happen to his body when you do the test so that sometimes it increases your hunger and sometimes it does not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T16:18:07-07:00","id":1455629,"title":"","content":"From the pitch given at conventions when V5 was first announced, my understanding is that the change from a blood pool to hunger dice was driven strictly by aesthetics, as the new developers never liked the idea of you having a gas tank. You could probably just use the old system without breaking anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-27-2021, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T00:33:14-07:00","id":1455644,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it comes from disdain for 'mana points' (which was never an issue I've seen raised previously, so that could be designer snobbery/personal taste).<br /> <br /> I think they also looked at modern games (and VTR1e's Atrocity Dice) and decided to crib a bit from those. It's very similar to Alien's Stress Dice, for example, so there may be converging tastes there or a shared heritage.<br /> <br /> Some people like the randomisation of Hunger and the blood. Some people don't see the need.<br /> <br /> In-character, I think it's just supposed to represent the unpredictability of the Beast. You never know when it's going to demand more of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T07:21:46-07:00","id":1455654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, it seems weird to me</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. A lot of game design in V5 is just weird in general. Your complaint about Hunger is also a conundrum people have raised before as well. Also the way you want to make and roleplay your character, brings up similar questions people have asked too; how can Vampires even exist as long as they do or even operate, if to satiate their hunger is to basically murder? This new mechanic from a retrospective standpoint, it really pokes some holes in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T12:22:25-07:00","id":1455728,"title":"","content":"From the description of the book, the hunger has nothing to do with the amount of blood in the body of the vampire. The way it's explained, exaltation may awake the beast inside and it will grow the instinct of the vampire to kill and satiate his thirst.<br /> But at the same time the book tell that a hunger at five mean that the vampire is too out of blood to use his disciplines.<br /> I swear i'm trying to find a litteral way to explain what happen when a vampire exalt his blood, but it's the beast instinct that affect the body<br /> &quot;That the beast that awake more and more each time you use your powers&quot; But in that case how do you explain the blood loss?<br /> &quot;your blood is consumed to activate your powers&quot; But why would it happen a time and not right after for the second power used?<br /> &quot;it's a way to show that the vampire get weaker with time or activities&quot; If he has luck he will gain only 2 hunger point during a fight with 4/5 powers used and if not during 10 minutes of stealth all his 3 powers he used has increased his hunger<br /> <br /> i think about it so much but nothing clear seems to fit that system and i'm blocking on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-28-2021, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T15:44:07-07:00","id":1455731,"title":"","content":"Any hunger, blood, humanity mechanic and so is done with the intent to emulate certain genre considerations of vampire media that served as inspirations for the game. However, these different sources have very different depictions of vampires. We have everything from irredeemable monsters lacking any compassion to very sympathetic vampires struggling to control their hunger. So whatever the game designers decide, they are pushing their thumb on one point of the scale they like best. That point may not be where you as a player group or ST wants to have their game. So feel free to make changes as needed to allow the kind of setting works best for you.<br /> <br /> The original version of the game really pushed the idea of Vampire of allowing players to explore the nature of evil and make choices to overcome it. Sometimes that meant games where it was impossible for someone to tell the PCs were supposed to be vampires at all, and there's been a reaction against that. I'm sympathetic to that reaction, but at the same time always liked characters like Hannibal King from Tomb of Dracula that showed a vampire who hated his condition and rejected it. Hannibal was a very cool character in a comic book that usually depicted vampires as completely awful so I've always thought that those elements can be combined.<br /> <br /> Since I don't play V5, I don't know how this hunger dice mechanic truly works in game so I can't give specific advice. But I encourage you to make what changes you can. Though I do think if you want to reduce it entirely so the PC can be completely humane and free of the Beast, you may want some kind of alternate mechanic that reflects the Beast is somehow subdued and thus not available in some beneficial way. Making it a real choice for the PC (I can do this, but at the cost of this) usually leads to better roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}